<section class="section border-t border-ink-primary" aria-labelledby="azure-case-heading"><div class="wrapper grid-edit"><div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-4"><p class="meta reveal"><span class="section-number" style="--accent:var(--color-pixel-orange)">The assignment</span></p><h2 id="azure-case-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.03em] mt-6 reveal">The cloud should simplify the business, not complicate it.</h2></div><div class="azure-case-copy col-span-12 md:col-span-7"><p class="azure-case-lead text-xl md:text-2xl text-ink-secondary reveal">Aging infrastructure, costly on-premises environments, fragmented cloud footprints, stalled migrations, and disconnected data platforms leave teams managing risk instead of shipping. Add security and compliance pressure, unpredictable spend, and slow release cycles, and the platform becomes the bottleneck. We design Azure environments around the workloads, controls, and operating discipline the business needs.</p><div class="azure-outcomes reveal reveal-delay-2"><div><span>Faster modernization</span><p>Move legacy workloads toward modern Azure architectures without unnecessary disruption.</p></div><div><span>Better visibility</span><p>Connect infrastructure, applications, data, security, and operations through a clearer cloud operating model.</p></div><div><span>Room to scale</span><p>An Azure foundation that supports new applications, data workloads, AI initiatives, and changing business needs.</p></div></div></div></div></section>

<section class="section section-statement" aria-labelledby="azure-services-heading"><div class="wrapper grid-edit"><div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-4"><p class="meta text-ink-inverse-secondary reveal"><span class="section-number" style="--accent:var(--color-pixel-yellow)">What we own</span></p><h2 id="azure-services-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.03em] mt-6 reveal">From the first cloud decision to the next optimization.</h2><p class="mt-6 text-ink-inverse-secondary max-w-md reveal reveal-delay-1">Bring us in for a defined workstream, or let us carry the whole transformation.</p></div><div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-8 md:pl-8"><ol class="azure-services"><li class="reveal reveal-delay-1"><span>01</span><div><h3>Azure strategy &amp; architecture</h3><p>Cloud readiness assessments, workload discovery with Azure Migrate, target architecture, Azure landing zones, governance and security planning, and a migration roadmap people can execute.</p></div></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-2"><span>02</span><div><h3>Cloud migration &amp; modernization</h3><p>Assessment, dependency mapping, wave planning, and workload migration by rehosting, replatforming, or refactoring, with cutover and rollback agreed in writing before anything moves.</p></div></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-3"><span>03</span><div><h3>Application modernization</h3><p>Azure App Service, Azure Kubernetes Service, Azure Container Apps, Azure Functions, Azure API Management, and cloud-native patterns applied where they pay back, not by default.</p></div></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-4"><span>04</span><div><h3>Data &amp; AI on Azure</h3><p>Microsoft Fabric, Azure Databricks, Azure SQL Database, Azure Cosmos DB, data integration, analytics, Azure AI Search, Azure Machine Learning, and Microsoft Foundry for intelligent applications and retrieval-augmented generation.</p></div></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-1"><span>05</span><div><h3>Security, identity &amp; governance</h3><p>Microsoft Entra ID, access management, Azure Policy, Microsoft Defender for Cloud, Microsoft Sentinel, Azure Key Vault, compliance controls, and a secure foundation that stays secure as the estate grows.</p></div></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-2"><span>06</span><div><h3>DevOps, optimization &amp; managed operations</h3><p>CI/CD with Azure DevOps or GitHub Actions, infrastructure as code with Bicep or Terraform, Azure Monitor observability, Microsoft Cost Management and FinOps, incident response, and continuous improvement.</p></div></li></ol></div></div></section>

<section id="engagement" class="azure-engagement section border-t border-ink-primary" aria-labelledby="azure-path-heading"><div class="wrapper"><div class="grid-edit"><div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-5"><p class="meta reveal"><span class="section-number" style="--accent:var(--color-pixel-green)">Delivery path</span></p><h2 id="azure-path-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.03em] mt-6 reveal">A clear sequence. No surprises at cutover.</h2></div><div class="azure-path-copy col-span-12 md:col-span-6"><p class="text-lg text-ink-secondary reveal">The exact shape depends on your estate. The order does not: establish the facts, make the architecture decisions early, validate hard, then stay accountable after the move.</p></div></div><ol class="azure-path"><li class="reveal reveal-delay-1"><b>01</b><h3>Discover</h3><p>Applications, infrastructure, data, dependencies, business requirements, risks, and cloud readiness.</p></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-2"><b>02</b><h3>Design</h3><p>Azure architecture, landing zone, security model, governance, networking, data strategy, and migration roadmap.</p></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-3"><b>03</b><h3>Migrate &amp; build</h3><p>Move workloads, modernize applications, stand up the platform, implement integrations, and build Azure-native capability.</p></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-4"><b>04</b><h3>Prove</h3><p>Performance, security, resilience, data integrity, monitoring, deployment processes, and operational readiness.</p></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-1"><b>05</b><h3>Operate</h3><p>Optimization, monitoring, FinOps, security improvements, incident support, managed services, and continuous modernization.</p></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="section azure-modules" aria-labelledby="azure-modules-heading"><div class="wrapper grid-edit"><div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-4"><p class="meta reveal"><span class="section-number" style="--accent:var(--color-pixel-purple)">Enterprise scope</span></p><h2 id="azure-modules-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.03em] mt-6 reveal">Where the platform earns its keep.</h2></div><div class="azure-modules__grid col-span-12 md:col-span-8 md:pl-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-px bg-ink-primary border border-ink-primary reveal reveal-delay-2"><div class="bg-bg-base p-7 md:p-8"><span class="meta">Cloud infrastructure</span><p>Azure Virtual Machines, virtual networks, storage, containers, and hybrid connectivity built as a foundation the business can scale on, not a collection of subscriptions.</p></div><div class="bg-bg-base p-7 md:p-8"><span class="meta">Application modernization</span><p>App Service, AKS, Container Apps, Functions, and APIs used to shorten release cycles and retire the applications that hold the business back.</p></div><div class="bg-bg-base p-7 md:p-8"><span class="meta">Data &amp; analytics</span><p>Microsoft Fabric, Azure Databricks, managed databases, data integration, and reporting that give leaders one reliable view instead of competing extracts.</p></div><div class="bg-bg-base p-7 md:p-8"><span class="meta">AI &amp; intelligent applications</span><p>Microsoft Foundry, Azure AI Search, Azure Machine Learning, retrieval-augmented generation, and agent patterns applied to use cases with a measurable business owner.</p></div><div class="bg-bg-base p-7 md:p-8"><span class="meta">Security &amp; governance</span><p>Identity, access, policy, threat detection, compliance evidence, and governance that keeps pace with change instead of slowing it down.</p></div><div class="bg-bg-base p-7 md:p-8"><span class="meta">DevOps &amp; cloud operations</span><p>CI/CD, infrastructure as code, observability, cost control, reliability engineering, and managed operations that keep the platform fast and predictable.</p></div></div></div></section>

<section class="section border-t border-ink-primary" aria-labelledby="azure-ways-heading"><div class="wrapper"><div class="grid-edit"><div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-5"><p class="meta reveal"><span class="section-number" style="--accent:var(--color-pixel-magenta)">Why Vertis Global</span></p><h2 id="azure-ways-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.03em] mt-6 reveal">Build it. Run&nbsp;it. Staff&nbsp;it.</h2></div><div class="azure-ways-copy col-span-12 md:col-span-6"><p class="text-lg text-ink-secondary reveal">Most Azure programs lose momentum between phases: the migration lands, then nobody owns the platform, or the team that built it moves on. We work across all three ways of engaging, so the handoffs are ours to manage.</p></div></div><ol class="azure-ways"><li class="reveal reveal-delay-1"><b>Build</b><h3>Projects</h3><p>Azure migration, modernization, application engineering, data, and AI projects with fixed scope and a written plan.</p><a href="/services/" class="link-edit">How projects run</a></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-2"><b>Run</b><h3>Managed services</h3><p>Azure cloud operations, monitoring, security, FinOps, application support, and optimization under a managed services agreement.</p><a href="/managed-services/cloud-operations/" class="link-edit">Cloud operations and FinOps</a></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-3"><b>Staff</b><h3>Staffing</h3><p>Azure architects, cloud engineers, DevOps engineers, data engineers, and developers placed into your team when you need capacity rather than a project.</p><a href="/staffing/" class="link-edit">Staffing options</a></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="section border-t border-ink-primary" aria-labelledby="azure-results-heading"><div class="wrapper grid-edit"><div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-4"><p class="meta reveal"><span class="section-number" style="--accent:var(--color-pixel-cyan)">Outcomes</span></p><h2 id="azure-results-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.03em] mt-6 reveal">What changes when Azure is run as a platform.</h2></div><div class="azure-results col-span-12 md:col-span-8 md:pl-8 reveal reveal-delay-2"><div><span>Modernized legacy environments</span><p>Workloads moved off aging infrastructure on a plan the business agreed to.</p></div><div><span>Application agility</span><p>Shorter release cycles on services that scale without a ticket.</p></div><div><span>Stronger cloud security</span><p>Identity, policy, and detection built in from the first subscription.</p></div><div><span>Infrastructure visibility</span><p>One view of what runs where, what it costs, and who owns it.</p></div><div><span>Data and AI readiness</span><p>A data foundation that AI initiatives can build on instead of waiting for.</p></div><div><span>Developer productivity</span><p>Pipelines, environments, and platform services teams no longer assemble themselves.</p></div><div><span>Cost control</span><p>Spend that is tagged, forecast, reviewed, and tied to an optimization backlog.</p></div><div><span>Scalable foundations</span><p>Landing zones and governance that absorb the next workload without a redesign.</p></div></div></div></section>

